  "title": "AI-Driven Mathematical Reasoning and Agentic Reasoning Synergy in Large Language Models",
  "summary": "This report investigates the integration of mathematical reasoning and agentic reasoning within large language models to enhance their capabilities, addressing misalignment in reasoning patterns between mathematical and agentic tasks. The findings suggest that synergistic approaches can improve reasoning depth and performance.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The method M2A synergizes mathematical and agentic reasoning by merging tasks along their null space, avoiding overfitting to superficial patterns.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Experiments demonstrate that M2A improves performance in real-world coding agent settings, increasing SWE-Bench Verified resolved rate from 44.0% to 51.2%.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "M2A operates without additional gradient updates and uses a simple knob to control reasoning depth.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
